      "obstacle_id": "o1",
      "text": "The system shall fuse forward‑facing radar and camera data to detect obstacles; if radar returns no detection due to blockage, the camera shall provide obstacle detection and the system shall issue a hazard alert within 0.2 seconds."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o2",
      "text": "The system shall guarantee that, from the moment an obstacle is detected to the initiation of braking, the total processing and actuation latency does not exceed 100 milliseconds."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o3",
      "text": "The system shall monitor driver gaze or head orientation and, if the driver’s eyes are off the forward road for more than 2 seconds, shall issue an audible and visual alert and automatically disengage Autopilot within 1 second."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o4",
      "text": "The system shall detect a hands‑off condition within 1 second, issue an escalating series of alerts, and if the driver does not resume a detectable hand‑on‑wheel torque within 3 seconds, shall disengage Autopilot and bring the vehicle to a safe stop."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o5",
      "text": "The system shall verify that the current road segment satisfies its Operational Design Domain (adequate lane‑mark visibility, limited cross‑traffic, and highway classification) before allowing Autopilot activation; if any criterion is not met, activation shall be prevented and a warning displayed."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o6",
      "text": "The system shall assign a confidence score to lane‑mark detection; when the confidence falls below 0.6, the system shall revert to a fallback lane‑keeping mode (using adjacent lane or driver input) and present a visual alert to the driver."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o8",
      "text": "The system shall employ multi‑modal driver‑engagement sensing (steering‑torque, grip sensor, and driver‑camera) and shall consider the driver engaged if any modality indicates hands‑on‑wheel above calibrated thresholds, thereby avoiding false hands‑off indications."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o7",
      "text": "The system shall continuously compute a safe following distance based on the lead vehicle’s instantaneous deceleration capability and shall adjust the TACC following‑distance setpoint within 0.5 seconds of detecting an abrupt speed reduction."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o9",
      "text": "The system shall classify low‑lying overpasses as obstacles using sensor fusion (camera, radar, and lidar) with a classification accuracy of at least 95 % in validation tests, and shall issue a warning or adjust speed when such an obstacle is detected."
    },
    {
      "obstacle_id": "o10",
      "text": "The system shall provide blind‑spot detection for all road users and, when a vehicle or motorcycle is present in the blind spot, shall issue a visual and audible alert and limit speed to a safe value until the driver confirms clearance."
    }
  ]
}

